  "message": "fix(core): don't turn truncated streamed tool-call arguments into a tool call\n\nOnce a stream has ended, re-derive tool calls from tool_call_chunks with\nJSON.parse, the rule the non-streaming path already applies. A call whose\narguments were cut off (output limit or a stream that just ends) lands in\ninvalid_tool_calls with the raw string instead of being repaired into a\ncomplete-looking call. Covers aggregation in BaseChatModel and providers\nthat stream inside _generate. Chunks seen while streaming keep the\npartial parse.\n\nFixes #11469",
