    "body": "### Submission checklist\n\n- [x] This is a bug, not a usage question.\n- [x] I added a clear and descriptive title that summarizes this issue.\n- [x] I used the GitHub search to find a similar question and didn't find it.\n- [x] I am sure that this is a bug in LangChain rather than my code.\n- [x] The bug is not resolved by updating to the latest stable version of LangChain (or the specific integration package).\n- [x] This is not related to the langchain-community package.\n- [x] I posted a self-contained, minimal, reproducible example. A maintainer can copy it and run it AS IS.\n\n### Package (Required)\n\n- [ ] langchain\n- [ ] langchain-openai\n- [ ] langchain-anthropic\n- [ ] langchain-classic\n- [x] langchain-core\n- [ ] langchain-model-profiles\n- [ ] langchain-tests\n- [ ] langchain-text-splitters\n- [ ] langchain-chroma\n- [ ] langchain-deepseek\n- [ ] langchain-exa\n- [ ] langchain-fireworks\n- [ ] langchain-groq\n- [ ] langchain-huggingface\n- [ ] langchain-mistralai\n- [ ] langchain-nomic\n- [ ] langchain-ollama\n- [ ] langchain-openrouter\n- [ ] langchain-perplexity\n- [ ] langchain-qdrant\n- [ ] langchain-typesafe\n- [ ] langchain-xai\n- [ ] Other / not sure / general\n\n### Related Issues / PRs\n\n- #39275: same report, auto-closed for submission format, not reviewed on the merits.\n- #38682 and #35743 (empty-args handling during streaming): adjacent but different.\n\n### Reproduction Steps / Example Code (Python)\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_core.language_models.chat_models import generate_from_stream\nfrom langchain_core.messages import AIMessageChunk\nfrom langchain_core.outputs import ChatGenerationChunk\n\nchunks = [\n    ChatGenerationChunk(message=AIMessageChunk(content=\"\", tool_call_chunks=[\n        {\"name\": \"edit_document\", \"args\": \"\", \"id\": \"call_1\", \"index\": 0, \"type\": \"tool_call_chunk\"}])),\n    ChatGenerationChunk(message=AIMessageChunk(content=\"\", tool_call_chunks=[\n        {\"name\": None, \"args\": '{\"operation\": \"replace\", \"blocks\": [{\"type\": \"hea',\n         \"id\": None, \"index\": 0, \"type\": \"tool_call_chunk\"}])),\n]\nmsg = generate_from_stream(iter(chunks)).generations[0].message\nprint(msg.tool_calls)\n# [{'name': 'edit_document', 'args': {'operation': 'replace', 'blocks': [{'type': 'hea'}]}, ...}]\nprint(msg.invalid_tool_calls)\n```\n\n### Error Message and Stack Trace (if applicable)\n\nNo error or stack trace. The bug is silent: a tool call whose arguments were cut off by the end of the stream comes out as a valid-looking tool call.\n\nRunning the reproduction above prints:\n\n```python\n  msg.tool_calls\n  [{'name': 'edit_document', 'args': {'operation': 'replace', 'blocks': [{'type': 'hea'}]}, 'id': 'call_1', 'type': 'tool_call'}]\n\n  msg.invalid_tool_calls\n  []\n```\nExpected: the truncated arguments land in invalid_tool_calls (raw string preserved) and tool_calls is empty.\n\n### Description\n\n`AIMessageChunk.init_tool_calls` parses every tool-call chunk's `args` with `parse_partial_json`. That's right while a stream is in flight. But it's also used for the final aggregated message: both the `chunk_position=\"last\"` chunk and the message that `generate_from_stream` builds for `invoke()` / `ainvoke()` with `streaming=True`.\n\nIf a stream ends partway through a tool call's arguments, partial parsing closes the open strings and brackets and returns a well-formed dict:\n- the call lands in `tool_calls`;\n- `invalid_tool_calls` stays empty;\n- the tool runs with half of its input.\n\nStreams end early more often than you'd think:\n- a provider or proxy closes the connection;\n- a gateway that reports a dropped upstream with `finish_reason: \"stop\"` (we saw this with an LLM proxy);\n- a timeout in an intermediary.\n\nOur concrete case: half of a document-edit payload was applied as a complete edit.\n\n### System Info\n\nSystem Information\n------------------\n> OS:  Darwin\n> OS Version:  Darwin Kernel Version 27.0.0: Tue Aug 11 21:06:40 PDT 2026; root:xnu-13432.1.9~1/RELEASE_ARM64_T6050\n> Python Version:  3.11.15 (main, Jun 23 2026, 15:46:51) [Clang 22.1.3 ]\n\nPackage Information\n-------------------\n> langchain_core: 1.6.12\n> langsmith: 0.14.9\n> langchain_protocol: 0.0.18\n> langchain_tests: 1.1.9\n\n### Social handles (optional)\n\n_No response_",
